我们不得不放弃基娜。

290
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:56,000
I mean, she's been jabbed, she's had an injection,
我的意思是，她已经接受了注射，已经得到治疗了。

291
00:21:56,000 --> 00:21:58,480
but whether they managed to get her into a truck or not
但他们是否真的能把她塞进卡车里呢？

292
00:21:58,480 --> 00:22:01,920
and get her to a thumber, I just haven't got a clue.
并把她送到某个地方……我完全不知道。

293
00:22:01,920 --> 00:22:04,400
I'll be amazed, to be honest, if they do.
说实话，如果他们真的做到了，我会很惊讶。

294
00:22:04,400 --> 00:22:07,920
But, three elephants in trucks,
但是，三头大象在卡车上……

295
00:22:07,920 --> 00:22:11,280
three elephants for those little babies from the Nairobi orphanage.
三头大象用来照顾内罗毕孤儿院里的那些小婴儿。

296
00:22:11,280 --> 00:22:13,200
I mean, that is just so important.
我的意思是，这非常重要。

297
00:22:13,200 --> 00:22:14,160
It's what it's all about.
这就是关键所在。

298
00:22:14,160 --> 00:22:17,520
They need the security of a bigger elephant right now.
目前它们需要一头更大的大象作为保护。

299
00:22:17,520 --> 00:22:19,680
They need a matriarch, somebody to rally around.
它们需要一位领袖，一个可以依靠的人。

300
00:22:19,680 --> 00:22:24,560
And the irony is, I was so sure that it was going to be Kina.
具有讽刺意味的是，我原本确信会是基娜来担任这个角色。

301
00:22:24,560 --> 00:22:28,160
To me, she seemed to be a leader, she was feisty,
对我来说，她似乎是个领导者，她很坚强有力。

302
00:22:28,160 --> 00:22:29,920
she was always bellowing her head off.
她总是大声地喊叫着。

303
00:22:29,920 --> 00:22:32,400
She always wanted to get back towards where Emily was,
她总是想回到艾米丽所在的地方。

304
00:22:32,400 --> 00:22:35,760
leading the troops and blow me if we hadn't had to leave her behind.
她带领着部队，如果我们不把她留下来的话，她就会攻击我们。

305
00:22:41,280 --> 00:22:50,960
The keepers have heard by radio that some of the trucks have left,
守军通过无线电得知，有些卡车已经出发了。

306
00:22:50,960 --> 00:22:53,600
so we hope that help is on its way
所以我们希望援助即将到来。

307
00:22:53,600 --> 00:22:56,400
for our bewildered and exhausted little Ellie's.
为了我们困惑又疲惫的小艾莉。

308
00:22:56,400 --> 00:23:01,760
Now, this is a very calm, relaxed, peaceful scene,
现在，这里是一幅非常平静、安宁的场景。

309
00:23:01,760 --> 00:23:04,480
but in 20 minutes' time, all that will change.
但20分钟后，一切都会改变。

310
00:23:04,480 --> 00:23:06,560
The trucks from Voy will arrive.
来自Voy的卡车将会到达。

311
00:23:06,560 --> 00:23:09,600
Now, no doubt, the elephants will be nervous,
现在，毫无疑问，大象们会感到紧张，

312
00:23:09,600 --> 00:23:11,920
because they're here the sound of the trucks,
因为这里有卡车的声音。

313
00:23:11,920 --> 00:23:14,720
but they also have the most amazing sense of communication,
但她们也拥有最出色的沟通能力，

314
00:23:14,720 --> 00:23:17,680
so it's highly likely that they will know that those elephants
因此，极有可能在它们甚至见到那些大象之前，

315
00:23:17,680 --> 00:23:19,600
are on their way before they even see them,
就能知道那些大象正在往它们所在的方向走来。

316
00:23:19,600 --> 00:23:21,280
so they'll also be excited.
所以他们也会感到兴奋。

317
00:23:21,280 --> 00:23:24,640
So this calmness isn't going to last.
这种平静不会持续下去。

318
00:23:24,640 --> 00:23:26,800
This is basically the calm before the storm.
这基本上就是暴风雨前的平静状态。

319
00:23:26,800 --> 00:23:35,920
What did they say, Bernard?
他们说了什么，伯纳德？

320
00:23:35,920 --> 00:23:37,360
The track is five minutes away.
列车还有五分钟到。

321
00:23:37,360 --> 00:23:38,560
Five minutes away.
五分钟就能到。

322
00:23:38,560 --> 00:23:41,360
So when we hear the truck, we're going to move the elephants closer.
所以，当我们听到卡车的声音时，我们就把大象拉近一点。

323
00:23:41,360 --> 00:23:42,000
Yeah.
是的。

324
00:23:42,000 --> 00:23:45,360
OK, we're down to the last leg now.
好的，现在就剩下最后一段路了。

325
00:23:45,360 --> 00:23:49,280
Of course, in the back of my mind, the whole way has been kinder.
当然，在心里，这一路过程都挺不错的。

326
00:23:49,280 --> 00:23:51,200
What has happened to kinder?
那么，那些“不错”的情况发生了什么？

327
00:23:51,200 --> 00:23:52,240
Is she on the road?
她正在路上吗？

328
00:23:52,240 --> 00:23:53,440
Will she join the herd?
她会加入大象群吗？

329
00:23:53,440 --> 00:23:56,720
Fingers crossed.
希望如此。

330
00:23:56,720 --> 00:24:00,960
Here we are.
我们到了。

331
00:24:00,960 --> 00:24:02,960
First question is, how are the Ellie's?
第一个问题是，埃莉们怎么样了？

332
00:24:03,760 --> 00:24:11,040
Come on, let's see what's going on.
来吧，让我们看看情况如何。

333
00:24:11,040 --> 00:24:13,520
Oh my goodness, they just hope everything's OK.
天哪，他们只是希望一切都没问题。

334
00:24:13,520 --> 00:24:14,400
So far, so good.
目前，一切都很顺利。

335
00:24:14,400 --> 00:24:15,840
Another drive was fantastic.
又一次驾驶过程非常棒。

336
00:24:15,840 --> 00:24:20,800
And here they come.
他们来了。

337
00:24:20,800 --> 00:24:32,160
This is where the keepers really come into their own.
这时，看护人才真正展现出他们的能力。

338
00:24:34,640 --> 00:24:36,640
Come in the Ellie's down and reassuring them
进入埃莉们所在的地方，安慰他们，

339
00:24:36,640 --> 00:24:38,800
in this strange new place is vital.
在这个陌生的新地方，这一点非常重要。

340
00:24:38,800 --> 00:24:42,880
Now this is Yatta.
现在，真是太棒了。

341
00:24:42,880 --> 00:24:45,600
She's the one that we had to sedate,
正是她需要被镇定下来。

342
00:24:45,600 --> 00:24:47,120
so I'm just hoping that she's OK.
所以我只希望她没事。

343
00:24:47,120 --> 00:24:49,440
She's bound to be a bit woozy.
她肯定会有些头晕的。

344
00:24:49,440 --> 00:24:55,280
OK, they're calling it to where the others are.
好了，他们正在指引其他人前往那里。

345
00:24:55,280 --> 00:24:58,800
Look at them nodding their heads.
看他们点头示意。

346
00:25:00,960 --> 00:25:04,160
It's just such a shame that only three of them have made it.
真可惜只有三个人成功到达了。

347
00:25:04,160 --> 00:25:09,520
Oh, fantastic, it's the other truck.
哦，太好了，那是另一辆卡车。

348
00:25:09,520 --> 00:25:13,280
It must be kinder, they must have kinder.
他们一定更友善，肯定更友善一些。

349
00:25:13,280 --> 00:25:14,880
That is so exciting.
真是令人兴奋。

350
00:25:14,880 --> 00:25:20,560
Now that is fantastic news.
这真是个好消息。

351
00:25:20,560 --> 00:25:24,880
There was me thinking, hey, how are these three going to feel?
我在想，这三个人会感觉如何呢？

352
00:25:24,880 --> 00:25:27,120
They've left one behind, how was kinder going to feel?
他们留下了一个人，那另一个人会感觉如何呢？

353
00:25:27,120 --> 00:25:28,880
She must be in the truck.
她一定在卡车里吧。

354
00:25:31,680 --> 00:25:33,040
And here comes the others.
然后其他人也来了。

355
00:25:33,040 --> 00:25:34,480
The others are coming over to have a look.
其他人也过来查看了。

356
00:25:34,480 --> 00:25:39,360
I can't believe they want to go anywhere near a truck.
我无法相信他们想靠近卡车。

357
00:25:39,360 --> 00:25:43,360
Kinder, kinder, kinder, kinder, kinder, kinder, kinder, kinder, kinder.
更友善、更友善、更友善、更友善、更友善、更友善、更友善、更友善、更友善。

358
00:25:43,360 --> 00:25:46,640
I can't believe they want to go anywhere near a truck.
我无法相信他们想靠近卡车。

359
00:25:46,640 --> 00:25:53,520
And here come the others. The others are coming over to have a look.
然后其他人也来了。其他人也过来查看了。

360
00:25:53,520 --> 00:26:00,560
I can't believe they want to go anywhere near a truck.
我无法相信他们想靠近卡车。

361
00:26:00,560 --> 00:26:02,240
Kinder must be calling today.
今天，孩子们一定在呼唤着。

362
00:26:02,240 --> 00:26:08,320
That's amazing.
太了不起了。

363
00:26:16,720 --> 00:26:18,880
One large step to freedom.
这是通往自由的一大步。

364
00:26:18,880 --> 00:26:21,520
Brave little elephants.
勇敢的小象们。

365
00:26:21,520 --> 00:26:32,160
Now, these big girls are here for a reason,
现在，这些大女孩出现是有原因的，

366
00:26:32,160 --> 00:26:34,640
and I think they're about to find out what it is.
我觉得她们即将知道那原因是什么。

367
00:26:34,640 --> 00:26:43,360
But all the trucks have arrived now,
不过，所有的卡车都已经到了，

368
00:26:43,360 --> 00:26:47,200
so the keepers need to move the orphans towards the stockade.
所以管理员需要把孤儿们送到围栏那里去。

369
00:26:47,200 --> 00:26:49,840
Now, I don't know how they're feeling, but I'm pretty excited.
现在，我不知道她们有什么感受，但我非常兴奋。

370
00:26:49,840 --> 00:26:53,360
This really is make or break time.
这真是一个决定成败的关键时刻。

371
00:26:53,360 --> 00:26:56,720
It's the babies, it's the babies from their own.
是那些婴儿，是它们自己的孩子。

372
00:26:56,720 --> 00:27:05,760
Look at that, that is just amazing.
看那，真是太神奇了。

373
00:27:05,760 --> 00:27:10,080
The incredibly calmly went up to see the bigger elephants.
它们异常平静地走向那些更大的大象。

374
00:27:10,720 --> 00:27:12,800
And now they just look a little bit for news.
现在它们只是稍微看看消息而已。

375
00:27:12,800 --> 00:27:16,560
You can see they're all using their trunks,
你可以看到它们都在使用它们的鼻子，

376
00:27:16,560 --> 00:27:18,880
just checking out one another, saying hello.
只是互相打量，互相问好。

377
00:27:18,880 --> 00:27:22,720
Kayla, hi, how did it go? Was it well?
凯拉，嗨，怎么样？还好吗？

378
00:27:22,720 --> 00:27:24,800
Yeah. How did it go?
是的。怎么样？

379
00:27:24,800 --> 00:27:28,320
Well, they were incredibly calm, actually.
其实，它们非常平静。

380
00:27:28,320 --> 00:27:29,280
I was surprised.
我很惊讶。

381
00:27:29,280 --> 00:27:31,920
I thought that they would be really excited and wound up,
我以为他们会非常兴奋，然后开始行动，

382
00:27:31,920 --> 00:27:35,280
but they very calmly walked towards the big elephants.
但实际上，他们却很平静地走向那些大象。

383
00:27:35,280 --> 00:27:37,520
They seemed to know they were there, but they were a bit like,
他们似乎知道有人的存在，但他们的反应就像这样：

384
00:27:37,520 --> 00:27:39,680
"Whoa, what are these big things?"
“哇，这些大东西是什么？”

385
00:27:40,240 --> 00:27:43,680
"It's incredible, isn't it? What they called to cry?"
“真是不可思议，对吧？它们在叫什么？”

386
00:27:43,680 --> 00:27:45,440
Don't worry.
不用担心。

387
00:27:45,440 --> 00:27:47,920
It's so sweet, it's so touching.
真是温馨又感人。

388
00:27:47,920 --> 00:27:52,880
See the way this one here, the big one.
看这个大象的样子吧。

389
00:27:52,880 --> 00:27:54,160
Yeah, that's my leaker in fact.
没错，那其实就是我的“泄露者”啊。

390
00:27:54,160 --> 00:27:56,240
And that's the pasture that the chalc is going over.
而那片草地，就是那只大象正在经过的地方。

391
00:27:56,240 --> 00:27:58,240
That's so gentle.
真是温柔极了。

392
00:27:58,240 --> 00:28:02,000
I think it's over to the elephants now, isn't it?
我觉得现在大象们已经平静下来了，对吧？

393
00:28:02,000 --> 00:28:03,440
I think so. Should we step back?
我也这么认为。我们该退后一点吗？

394
00:28:03,440 --> 00:28:08,080
After everything they've been through in the past few days,
经过过去几天所经历的一切之后，

395
00:28:08,080 --> 00:28:11,360
it's wonderful to see all these elephants starting to relax.
看到这些大象开始放松下来真是太好了。

396
00:28:11,360 --> 00:28:14,960
They still have a long way to go
它们还有很长的路要走，

397
00:28:14,960 --> 00:28:17,280
before they really bond as a herd,
才能真正团结成一个群体。

398
00:28:17,280 --> 00:28:21,440
but hopefully just for the moment everyone can draw a breath
但希望至少现在大家都能喘口气，

399
00:28:21,440 --> 00:28:23,280
before the next big adventure begins.
在下一个重大冒险开始之前。

400
00:28:23,280 --> 00:28:30,240
Tomorrow on Elephant Diaries,
明天在《大象日记》中，

401
00:28:30,240 --> 00:28:33,360
rescued babies flooding filling the empty stables
被救出的婴儿们填满了空着的马厩。

402
00:28:33,360 --> 00:28:34,640
at the Nairobi nursery.
在内罗毕的育婴室里。

403
00:28:36,160 --> 00:28:38,560
In solvos, something's upsetting, Emily.
在索尔沃斯，有事情让艾米丽感到不安。

404
00:28:38,560 --> 00:28:43,440
And at the new release site, there's big trouble.
而在新出生婴儿的安置地点，也出现了大麻烦。

405
00:28:43,440 --> 00:28:46,880
I woke up this morning feeling on top of the world,
今天早上我醒来时，感觉仿佛站在世界之巅，

406
00:28:46,880 --> 00:28:48,880
really excited about seeing the ellies again,
非常期待能再次见到那些婴儿们，

407
00:28:48,880 --> 00:28:50,080
and of course the keepers,
当然还有那些照顾者们，

408
00:28:50,080 --> 00:28:52,400
and one word has changed all of that,
而有一个词改变了这一切，

409
00:28:52,400 --> 00:28:55,200
and that word is outrageous.
那个词就是“令人愤怒”。
